{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/cargo.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:58:57.162413Z","id":"e98468623bef723e135e7b3efdf67907cd00ae2e14a87236bb87fa267e8aa6b8","body":{"detail":"The CARGO and CLAX_BUILD_COMMIT rustc_env entries justify themselves by \"(spec §5.3)\" and \"(spec B13)\". No file under docs/ (bazel.md, contract.md, usage.md, verification.md, follow-ups.md) has a section 5.3 or an item B13 about Bazel, so a reader cannot find the rule these lines enforce. docs/bazel.md (\"Differences from Cargo\") is where line 112 already points for the same kind of reason.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"d5091a54e791e06f25e7ed20d5fecfeb8311b111354adaa24e95fb45b7644d1c"},"suggested_fix":"Replace each citation with the reason itself or a pointer into docs/bazel.md (for example: \"no cargo runs under Bazel, so a test that falls back to running it fails loudly\" and \"a Bazel build is not stamped with a commit, so cached outputs are shared across commits\").","summary":"Comments cite \"spec §5.3\" and \"spec B13\", which no document in the repository defines","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/cargo.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:47.489629Z","id":"13d5e3df4d8a2fddf82cd4a38baba5a4e91dc9805ae751d28629b9750d563639","body":{"detail":"bazel/cargo.bzl:100 \"(spec §5.3)\" and :102 \"(spec B13)\". `grep -rn 'B13\\|§5\\.3' docs AGENTS.md README*` prints nothing; the only \"5.3\" matches in docs/ are timings (docs/bazel.md:366, :400; docs/verification.md:1057, :1214, :1218).","kind":"comment","references":"e98468623bef723e135e7b3efdf67907cd00ae2e14a87236bb87fa267e8aa6b8","summary":"confirmed: \"spec §5.3\" and \"spec B13\" cite nothing in the repository","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/cargo.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:57:11.671415Z","id":"73cb27087d4386743b3018a1c5fcd19a5bfb39d8e0487d7ca6160c820ac358f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:72432fb86","summary":"Fixed: the cargo.bzl comments give their reasons and point to docs/bazel.md 'Differences from Cargo' instead of spec section numbers.","supersedes":"e98468623bef723e135e7b3efdf67907cd00ae2e14a87236bb87fa267e8aa6b8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
